{"kind":"artifact","text":"notes/2026-10-04-scope-and-replay-contract.md at exact 3b3e394fc6807c33211ac80db813621253c38f5c on request/scope-contract-r15, under promise git:sha1…2b59050 on request git:sha1…dfc2ad7\n\nScope and replay contract, revision 23 at 3b3e394fc6807c33211ac80db813621253c38f5c on request/scope-contract-r15, for my request 22fc1a93, answering the checker's changes-requested verdict 675776bc on a1c709e4. Primary subject: notes/2026-10-04-scope-and-replay-contract.md. Design only; nothing was run but edit and count scripts outside the repository. The one finding is repaired, and the planner's four answers (2d3fa911) are recorded as decided. A binding selector must use an index: an item type in platform data may declare one to four indexed slots, each fixed and required and of one of seven reference or digest types, so an item has one key for life; a binding selector mark states its index and the message field that supplies the key, whose type must equal the slot's; the validator refuses a binding selector with no index, an undeclared index or a key of another type, by the existing name bound-source; the rule is given only the items the index returns for that key at this head, live and final, in item order, at most eight, with the message's fields, and picks one of them or none. The index is derived state: one row per item written in the opening transaction, complete at every head, rebuilt by folding in a replay, held in no checkpoint and counted in no dimension; its work is at most nine rows and eight items, with any charge owed to R4. The note states the owner's requirement as a requirement: it does not say the earlier scan was unbounded, since the item budget bounded it. Three choices are the author's and the reviewer should look at them first: more than eight matches is a fault, which never ends by itself because keys are fixed and final items are retained; only seven slot types may be indexed; and index or key on a mark that is not a binding selector is refused. Other selectors at place 2 are not required to use an index. Witness 18.53 now has 25 cases, with new ones for no index, an undeclared index, a key of the wrong type, two matches of which one is final, completeness at the head, nine matches, and a whole-reference match among 40 others. One fact differs from what the author was told: by the adopted authority rows an operation has at most one publication, so the several-match rule is stated but unused in the adopted case. The authority note owes the index on the publication's operation slot and its statement by the selector. The sweep found the finding in six places and three planner answers still written as questions in four; all are repaired. This revision is not small: 641 lines added and 77 removed in the note. Counts by script: 61 source rows, 69 points, 54 witnesses. Both pinned lane definitions were walked by script and declare none of the new members.","body":{"commit":"3b3e394fc6807c33211ac80db813621253c38f5c","path":"notes/2026-10-04-scope-and-replay-contract.md"}}